  "result": "Perfect! I found the source file that decides the numbering for newly created issues.\n\nThe `nextIssueNumber` function in `issue-repository.ts` (lines 292-304) is responsible for determining what number a newly created issue is given. \n\nHere's how it works:\n\n1. It queries the database to find the **maximum issue number** for the specific project within the organization\n2. It returns that max + 1 (or 1 if no issues exist yet)\n\nThe key lines are:\n```typescript\nexport async function nextIssueNumber(\n  orgId: OrgId,\n  projectId: ProjectId,\n): Promise<number> {\n  const row = getDb()\n    .select({ value: sql<number | null>`max(${issues.number})` })\n    .from(issues)\n    .where(\n      and(orgPredicate(issues.orgId, orgId), eq(issues.projectId, projectId)),\n    )\n    .get();\n  return (row?.value ?? 0) + 1;\n}\n```\n\nThis function ensures that:\n- Each project has its own independent counter (filtered by `projectId`)\n- The counter is scoped per organization (filtered by `orgId`)\n- This allows two projects in the same organization to each start at 1 and maintain separate numbering sequences\n\nANSWER: src/server/repositories/issue-repository.ts",
